model above represents one whole. From left to right, what numbers are missing from the division problem below?\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\,\\,}÷\\frac{1}{3}=\\boxed{\\,\\,}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In the model, there are $6$ shapes. Each shape consists of $3$ pieces that each represent $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a whole. There are $18$ pieces in total.\n\nThe model tells us that when we divide $6$ wholes into thirds, we will be left with $18$ pieces.\n\nHence, the division problem is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\,6\\,}÷\\frac{1}{3}=\\boxed{\\,18\\,}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing numbers are $6$ and $18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed8053e5-f273-56f2-bfb6-294f936d9701" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Representing a Division Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d0ff9e0-35db-5bc9-91f1-79e039622baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a0/a084209041e41554c744914bf42692c9d6cc77c3d86bb85747c1c62df15aab99.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509748} {:answer/id #uuid "7090b097-239e-5212-88fd-47671d2450fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/20/20895cf6185b627cf2081cb9afd248ff1bb3a8b11a988807bfb1a04ada2302f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509918} {:answer/id #uuid "9abe1a9b-a332-59c0-ab49-37957cb6cdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ecb4ff70a833b96a4f0e42ae14e3afff36c5a3fa656fedf45830fe64791db738.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510012} {:answer/id #uuid "cfbebdf1-3a63-5465-be64-fa925058ad05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d0/d08c2ac302acf38baa05c091c52a0a1d8fd89570989503f028529e0fa2cd9ff9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510128} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc48ef6-a7f8-5213-bda3-913460dbb747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/29ab6ef1e10eab020a25bec6c949bebeaf0c2cb5cb77db125f84fd6dd6c88129.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9abe1a9b-a332-59c0-ab49-37957cb6cdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ecb4ff70a833b96a4f0e42ae14e3afff36c5a3fa656fedf45830fe64791db738.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510012} :answer-field/id #uuid "546f4173-148e-5f1a-a1fc-5d267635ba7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a352b711-8af2-5a66-960f-d91f88b29c96" :question/math-academy-id "q-92127" :question/problem "Which model represents the division problem below?\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{8}=16\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate $2÷\\frac{1}{8}$, we need to divide each of $2$ wholes into $8$ equal parts, as shown below. This gives us the corresponding model for the given division problem.\n\n![](images/80/80d6548bd656ccfd0e4a2cd3dadd52671f7c9cfa648faf9ed293463adf3a92ba.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $2\\times 8=16$ pieces in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e310e4-b8a2-5327-b4e6-fd71b6783e3a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Whole Numbers by Unit Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e9be780-5147-51ee-b002-a0f63e5a12b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509853} {:answer/id #uuid "68111c37-72e6-5fc9-be07-6a3b54ac4ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509905} {:answer/id #uuid "9cba4bf1-c6c7-5edd-8528-71868f7bbfb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510015} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec836ed-be04-5f5e-89ff-824aa2643569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510019} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4a7e45-1247-5586-a96f-798ff42a6b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cba4bf1-c6c7-5edd-8528-71868f7bbfb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510015} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba16430-0b0e-51ab-956c-4e4440ad03c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4afa323a-6ccb-55bc-8693-1338e0d62847" :question/math-academy-id "q-92138" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4af3047f22d112fd3b1c2689ffacc50a1ce3d53dc458327ba25038f448de9c61.png)\n\nThe model above represents $3$ wholes. Use this model to calculate the value of $3÷\\frac{1}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate $3÷\\frac{1}{7}$, we need to divide each of $3$ wholes into $7$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/19/19b5902c790191dff44c240bb518feeeea9f9ffe5c0c440ca94b59344b78e1eb.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $3\\times 7=21$ pieces in total. \n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{1}{7}=21\n$$"}]}
